SpiderX overlay patch 2 for ros-controls/gz_ros2_control tag 0.7.15
(commit bfc5845aa7f0250cbc384773dba5c9847d609b95), package directory gz_ros2_control/.
Applies after 0001-plugin-node-parameter-overrides.patch.

Problem: on shutdown (SIGINT), controller_manager 2.51.0's pre-shutdown callback removes its
own node from the plugin's executor. The 0.7.15 destructor then calls
executor_->remove_node(controller_manager_) again; rclcpp 16.0.13 throws std::runtime_error
"Node needs to be associated with an executor." from the destructor, and the Gazebo server
aborts (SIGABRT). Seen with the stock and the overlay library (S2 runs of 2026-10-29 and
2026-10-30).

Upstream: humble commit 366137556d1fe3adf327a99b17261dcde549e655 (2025-09-26),
"Don't remove the node at destruction (#683) (#686)", cherry-picked from
90c951871312862879f66d2ceb8f92b7ecc8dc55, released in 0.7.17. It deletes the removal and the
early return on a missing controller manager, and keeps executor_->cancel() and
thread_executor_spin_.join().

Change (the upstream fix, plus guards for a partial Configure()):
- The destructor no longer removes the controller-manager node. It calls
  stop_executor_thread(): cancel the executor if it exists, join the spin thread if it is
  joinable. Upstream 0.7.17 would dereference a null executor, or join a thread that never
  started, when Configure() returned early.
- Offline gtest test_shutdown_teardown (no Gazebo): the plugin destroyed before Configure();
  the second removal throwing after the controller manager's self-removal (the defect); the
  teardown after that shutdown sequence, while spinning, without a spin thread, without an
  executor, and twice. Each spinning case first waits until the executor is spinning: a cancel()
  issued before spin() starts is lost in rclcpp (spin() sets its own flag), which is a property
  of the test set-up, not of the teardown.

Apply from the repository root, after patch 1: git apply <this file>
